melody:
# Verse 1 ("I" and "It" are sung on a two-note pickup G-A)
I come from Al-a-ba-ma with my ban-jo on my knee,
G4/ ~A4/ B4 D5 D5. E5/ D5 B4 G4. A4/ B4 B4 A4 G4 A4(3)
I'm goin' to Lou-si-an-a, my true love for to see.
G4 B4 D5 D5. E5/ D5 B4 G4. ~A4/ B4 B4 A4 A4 G4(3)
It rained all night the day I left, the wea-ther it was dry,
G4/ ~A4/ B4 D5 D5. E5/ D5 B4 G4. A4/ B4 B4 A4 G4 A4(3)
the sun so hot I froze to death; Su-san-na, don't you cry.
G4 B4 D5 D5. E5/ D5 B4 G4. A4/ B4 B4 A4 A4 G4(3)

# Chorus
Oh! Su-san-na, oh don't you cry for me,
G4 C5(2) C5(2) E5(2) E5(2) D5 D5 B4 G4 A4(3)
I come from Al-a-ba-ma with my ban-jo on my knee.
